# G3AQ characteristic-zero promotion contract

## Purpose

`UST.G3AQ` promotes the selected finite `F_(101^6)` response rank only after
`G3AP`, `G3AM`, and `G3AN` are closed. This note isolates the field-change
argument. A p-adic coefficient field is not silently identified with `C`.

**Current status:** discharged. The hash-current G3AN packet has
`rank(D0)=33`, `rank(E)=89` and a unit `122 x 122` block certificate; the
G3AQ builder and independent verifier promote rank 122 and left nullity 126.
This document remains the proof contract explaining that promotion.

## Universal regular locus

Fix the q79 Cayley ambient, Cox degree `beta`, and the full section polytope.
Let `U_reg` be the rational coefficient locus on which the Cayley
hypersurface is regular on every toric orbit and has full Newton polytope.
G3AO proves that the selected special-fiber member lies on the corresponding
regular locus. Properness of the relative toric ambient then proves that any
integral lift with this special fiber has regular generic fiber.

Over `C`, Mavlyutov Theorem 4.4 identifies the selected graded `R1` piece with
the appropriate open-torus Hodge piece. Danilov--Khovanskii computes its
Hodge--Deligne dimension from the common Newton polytope. Therefore this
dimension is constant on `U_reg(C)`. The old B72 member is used only to show
that the common dimension is nonzero; none of its response entries is used.

## Descent from C

The selected graded `R1` piece is the cokernel of a finite matrix with entries
in the rational coordinate ring of `U_reg`. Write its common complex rank as
`r`. The regular full-support coefficient locus is a reduced open subscheme
of an affine coefficient space. Constancy on all of its complex points makes
the relevant larger minors vanish as functions and makes the selected-size
minors have no common zero. Equivalently, after base change to `C`,

```text
Fitt_(r-1)(R1) = 0,
Fitt_r(R1) = O.
```

For a finitely presented module these are precisely the Fitting conditions
for finite local freeness of rank `r`, and Fitting ideals commute with base
change. Since `Q -> C` is faithfully flat, both ideal equalities descend to
`Q`. They persist after base change to any characteristic-zero field. In
particular, the selected 101-adic fraction field has the same dimension; no
embedding of that field into `C` is used.

This is the required bridge:

```text
complex polytope theorem
  -> empty rational Fitting rank-jump loci
  -> every characteristic-zero regular full-polytope fiber
  -> selected 101-adic generic fiber
```

It is a dimension transport, not a coefficient or matrix-entry transport.

## Unit-minor promotion

G3AH supplies a free rank-123 integral incidence kernel. Removing the
primitive radial line gives a free rank-122 projective tangent module, and the
122 G3AL residue directions lift to a basis by Nakayama. G3AP and the
nonzero `R1` dimension make the ordinary top module free of rank one over the
selected DVR.

G3AM and G3AN then provide one explicit `122 x 122` minor whose determinant is
nonzero modulo 101. Any integral lift of that determinant is a unit in the
DVR. Hence the characteristic-zero response has rank at least 122; its domain
has rank 122, so its rank is exactly 122 and the 248-row left nullity is 126.

## Boundary

G3AQ does not define or evaluate `beta_C`. It does not select a unique member
of the 123-dimensional G3AJ residue ball, construct the physical HYM metric,
or close the Hull--Strominger endpoint. Those remain later source theorems.

